[agent] ### Features engineered (model-independent, stored in the FG)
[agent] - `amount`, `log_amount`, `hour`, `is_night`
[agent] - `amount_ratio` (vs the card's mean spend from labelled history)
[agent] - `geo_distance` (haversine from the card's home location)
[agent] - `velocity_1h`, `velocity_24h` (trailing per-card transaction counts, past-only — no leakage)
[agent] - 10 category one-hot columns
[agent] The strongest signals were amount (fraud avg $154 vs $26) and night-hour timing (00–04 fraud rate ~12% vs <1% daytime), which alone drive most of the discrimination. Card-reference stats (mean amount, home location) are computed from the labelled history only and applied identically to the scoring set, so train/score feature engineering is consistent and the same code path scores every row.
